# API module organization

Treat `apps/api/src/nodes` as the **canonical template** for new and refactored
feature modules in the API app: structure, naming, layering, and readability.

Also apply `.cursor/rules/code-organization.mdc` and Cortex style
(`.cursor/skills/cortext-style/SKILL.md`).

## Layout

```text
<feature>/
  index.ts                 # Public barrel — module + services others may import
  <feature>.module.ts
  <feature>.controller.ts  # Or controller/ when multiple HTTP surfaces
  <feature>.service.ts
  repository/
    <feature>.repository.ts   # Port (interface) + token + Impl in one file
  models/                  # Domain models; JSDoc on every property
  parameters/              # App-layer inputs (not protocol DTOs)
    <operation>/
      <operation>-parameters.ts
  error/
    error.ts               # Folder-scoped module errors only
  filter/
    exception.filter.ts    # Maps module errors → HTTP at the controller boundary
  mapper/                  # Optional — protocol/DB ↔ domain
```

Omit folders the feature does not need. Prefer this shape over flat
`*-repository.ts` next to the service when adding or reshaping modules.

## Layering

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|-------|------|----------|
| Controller | HTTP, protocol Zod via `ZodValidationPipe`, `@UseFilters` | Business rules, Prisma |
| Service | Lifecycle / domain rules; throws typed module errors | Leak DB / transport shapes |
| Repository | Persistence port + Impl; returns domain models | HTTP concerns |
| Filter | `ModuleError` → status + `{ statusCode, code, message }` | Catch unrelated errors |
| Models / parameters | Domain + app inputs | Inline in service/controller |

## Repository pattern (from nodes)

- Export `SYMBOL` token, `interface` port, and `*RepositoryImpl`.
- Wire in the module with `{ provide: TOKEN, useClass: Impl }`.
- Inject the port with `@Inject(TOKEN)`, not the concrete class.
- Map DB failures to module errors with `{ cause }`.

## Errors and HTTP

- Base `*ModuleError` with stable `code` in `error/error.ts`.
- Service: domain/not-found style errors for callers.
- Repository: operational `*FailedError` for persistence failures.
- Controller-scoped filter `@Catch(ModuleError)`; do not leak Prisma details.

## Naming: Request vs Parameters

| Suffix | Meaning | Lives in |
|--------|---------|----------|
| `*Request` / `*Response` | Validated inbound/outbound HTTP or protocol DTOs (Zod schemas, `@cortex/protocol`) | protocol package or local schema next to the controller pipe |
| `*Parameters` | App-layer operation args after the controller has extracted/assembled them (service / repository inputs) | `<feature>/parameters/` |
| models | Domain entities, persisted shapes, mapping results | `<feature>/models/` |

Do not use `*Input` for service-entry bags. Example: `GitHubWebhookHandleParameters`,
not `GitHubWebhookHandleInput`. When the body itself needs schema validation,
that validated type is a `*Request` (e.g. `RegisterNodeRequest`); the service may
still take `*Parameters` if the app layer reshapes or enriches the request.

## Readability

- Thin controllers: validate → service → protocol response parse.
- MARK sections, constructor JSDoc, public method contracts.
- Feature `index.ts` exports only what other modules should import.
